## Session 22 summary

**scaling_curve root cause found and fixed (env-level, verified):** The multi-node degradation was NOT mxfs lock contention — the CAW slot table after a parallel 2-node rsync showed near-zero churn (AG slots all gen=1). The real cause: **any ≥2 concurrent large iSCSI transfers collapsed ~9× in per-command latency**, reproducible with raw `dd` (no FS), even same-initiator and even on clyde's loopback initiator. Proven via `ss -ti`: open-iscsi sets an explicit SO_RCVBUF (512KB default `tcp.window_size`), which Ubuntu's `net.core.rmem_max=212992` clamps AND which disables TCP window autotuning — the advertised window pinned at ~91-418KB, so >1MB in flight thrashed on window stalls/delayed ACKs/retransmits. Fix: `rmem_max/wmem_max=16MB` + `node.conn[0].tcp.window_size=16777216`, applied persistently to clyde and all 16 nodes via new in-tree `scripts/tune_iscsi_tcp.sh` (RULE 3). Verified: local dual 1M streams 122MB/s→1.9GB/s; cross-node dual 217MB/s→1.83GB/s aggregate.

**mxfs CAW hot-path reductions also landed this session (v0.5.3, build `8831EAED`, deployed test1/test2):** slot reads during a 2-node rsync dropped 9716→2715 and solo-on-2-node wall 4622→3504ms via: (1) waiter-side UDP BAST re-send every 100ms while blocked + holder idle disk-poll relaxed 200ms→1s when UDP is up + rotating >256-held coverage window (`dlm/dlm_caw.c/h`); (2) slot-index hint cache in the CAW ctx, content-validated single-read fast path in `find_slot_skip`; (3) claim-race rescan skipped for hash-base claims (1441→24 reads); (4) Bug-93 CAS compare-buffer reuse (705→0 reads); (5) P108/P106 dir held-verify throttle 100ms→1s (`xfs/xfs_mxfs_dlm.c`); (6) all 10 P15-INSTR AG logs gated behind `mxfs.instr`.

**Next session:** re-run `tests/criteria/scaling_curve.sh --nodes 16` (expect the flat ~7-8s multi-node walls to drop sharply with the transport fixed); then re-run cache_coherency + single_node_paired to confirm no regression from the v0.5.3 CAW changes (esp. the 1s held-verify throttle), run `posix_semantics_multi16`, then the full `verify_ship.sh` gate. Criteria marker NOT written — gate not yet green.

